{"task_id": "HumanEval/54", "solution": "def _extract_unique_chars(s: str) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the set of unique characters from a given string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return set(s)\n\ndef same_chars(s0: str, s1: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if two words have the same characters.\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddeddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('dddddddabc', 'abcd')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('eabcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabce')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddddabc')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_chars_s0 = _extract_unique_chars(s0)\n    unique_chars_s1 = _extract_unique_chars(s1)\n    return unique_chars_s0 == unique_chars_s1"}
